-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Starquake
  Publisher   Bubble Bus Software, 1985
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Starquake (1985)(Bubble Bus).z80
  MD5         b94691b08d31386d3e5661d04e6c164f

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Pace        original (-0.12% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless on the
              NextZXOS v2.09 card, against the plain build of the same file;
              probe 0xC5A9, keys applied after the game's last read; the seed
              at room entry 0xA489 fixed in both arms; 90 state addresses
              equal at every update)

  Changes     1.1: the game holds the original's pace: 1.0 lost single frames
              in busy rooms and up to 44 frames in a lost life. Half of the
              figures' plot now runs at 28 MHz, and the game's own frame sync
              gives back what is over.

  Note        No outline on the figures: the owner chose that for this mostly
              black game. The patch writes the whole alt ROM image, which
              fixed a crash on the define-keys screen. Plays at the original's
              pace, measured with the same input and enemy seeds in 6 runs of
              590 to 1,000 game updates in JNext: overall -0.12 to +0.00%,
              quiet scenes -0.06 to +0.03%, busy scenes -0.23 to +0.02%,
              slowest stretch of 20 updates +0.5%; faster stretches down to
              -4.9% are single updates where the original itself lags. A lost
              life takes the original's 249 frames (1.0: up to 292). Known
              issues: the same keys can give different enemies from the
              unpatched game's, because the game seeds its random numbers from
              the frame counter; beeper notes get 3 to 8% more edges a second
              than the original's, counted, not listened to. Missing: no
              Enhanced colour set (rated moderate); cheats unplayed by a
              person; not reached in testing: high-score name entry, the core
              assembly and the ending; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite energy
   3  No aliens
   4  Immunity

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

